Subject: [PATCH 06/12] Accept links typed without https://, and say so when a
 link is refused
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"tiktok.com/@cook/…" was refused. On a recipe that replaced the whole
page with an error; on a place the sheet just sat there with the 400
in the console. Bare addresses now get https:// added (javascript: and
friends are still refused), and a refusal shows under the field.

